+// lexInputTokens lexes the given source and returns both the "native"
+// tokens (those from hclsyntax) and the equivalent "writer" tokens.
+//
+// To do our work, we use the native tokens to match against source ranges
+// in the AST, but ultimately produce slices from our sequence of writer
+// tokens, which contain only *relative* position information that is more
